WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 5.3 · Internal Systems & Operations
Processes, SOPs and process ownership

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Write down repeated, risky processes so anyone can follow them, with one owner.

3
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.600
1. Map trigger, steps, roles, records and exceptions.

4
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.200
2. Ask the people doing the work what really happens.

5
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:22.200
3. Give each process one owner and a review date.

6
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:23.800
An example: Vanita Weavers Cooperative (Cooperative · member-owned, India)

7
00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:31.000
“Pieces totalled each Friday, checked by Meera against the register, co-signed with the treasurer, paid by transfer within 15 days.”

8
00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:33.400
You create a process register and map one priority process.

9
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:37.400
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

10
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:42.000
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
